name: kr-imported-generic-fold-tuple-acc
backends: [int, js, jvm, v2]
known-red: "jvm — NOT this case's subject. std/aggregator.ssc carries fmix64, whose 64-bit Long literals run-jvm transpiles into a 32-bit Int context; that is the pre-existing int-width non-conformance already declared on std-aggregator and std-aggregator-approx. The fold this case is about is GREEN on int and js. Remove when int-width is fixed."
---

# An imported generic fold over a TUPLE accumulator

Executable record of BUGS.md `imported-generic-fold-with-a-tuple-accumulator-presents-one-component`,
which had no gate.

`ZipAgg` accumulates a pair. A locally-written fold over it produces both components; the same
fold reached through the imported `runAggregator` presents only one. The case runs BOTH so the
contrast is the assertion — a case with only the imported call would not show that the
aggregator itself is fine.

**RE-MEASURED 2026-08-31: the reported defect no longer reproduces.** Both calls answer `(4, 2)`
on int and js. The entry's diagnosis said the failure follows POSITION rather than the module
boundary — whichever generic fold runs first is the truncated one — so this was checked in the
order that mattered: imported-first, local-first, and three imported calls in a row. All correct.
The case is kept as the regression gate the entry never had.

```scalascript
[Aggregator, runAggregator, ZipAgg, SumAgg, CountAgg](std/aggregator.ssc)

def runLocal[In, Acc, Out](xs: List[In], agg: Aggregator[In, Acc, Out]): Out =
  val acc = xs.foldLeft(agg.monoid.empty)((a, in) => agg.monoid.combine(a, agg.prepare(in)))
  agg.present(acc)

def main(): Unit =
  val xs = List(3.0, 1.0)
  val agg = ZipAgg(SumAgg(), CountAgg[Double]())
  println(runLocal(xs, agg).toString)
  println(runAggregator(xs, agg).toString)
```
